From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:27:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: qcom-hw: CPRh: don't request required-OPP linking

The CPR3 attach_dev callback populates the shared CPU OPP table while
the power domain attaches; devm_pm_domain_attach_list() with
PD_FLAG_REQUIRED_OPP then calls dev_pm_opp_set_config() on the already
populated table, which WARNs and fails with -EBUSY, so no cpufreq
policy gets registered on MSM8998.

OSM does the DVFS in hardware and the driver only reads the CPR-adjusted
voltages from the CPU OPP table, so drop PD_FLAG_REQUIRED_OPP.
---
 drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
index 5bee8f110eb6..8d6998dafa73 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
@@ -296,10 +296,16 @@ static struct {
 } qcom_cpufreq;
 
 static const char * const cprh_genpd_names[] = { "perf" };
+/*
+ * No PD_FLAG_REQUIRED_OPP: the CPR3 attach_dev callback populates the (shared)
+ * CPU OPP table while the genpd attaches, and dev_pm_opp_set_config() refuses
+ * an already populated table. OSM does the DVFS in hardware; we only read the
+ * CPR-adjusted voltages, so the required-opps link is not needed.
+ */
 static const struct dev_pm_domain_attach_data cprh_pd_data = {
 	.pd_names = cprh_genpd_names,
 	.num_pd_names = ARRAY_SIZE(cprh_genpd_names),
-	.pd_flags = PD_FLAG_DEV_LINK_ON | PD_FLAG_REQUIRED_OPP,
+	.pd_flags = PD_FLAG_DEV_LINK_ON,
 };
 static unsigned long cpu_hw_rate, xo_rate;
 static bool icc_scaling_enabled;
-- 
